# Default heat is a forward (causal) EWMA of the daily counts, half-life
# SMOOTH_HALF_LIFE_DAYS, in commit units: v_d = c_d + r·v_{d-1},
# r = 2^(-1/half-life) — the textbook λ=1-r EWMA times 1/λ, so a lone commit
# still reads as 1 on its day and halves every half-life after. 7 days read
# as over-smoothed under the log color scale (Joseph, 2026-10-16).
# The cell shows v − SMOOTH_FLOOR (zero below it): subtracting rather than
# cutting lets the decay fade continuously to white instead of jumping from
# t≈0.06 to zero, and still bounds how long the decay stays visible.
# The birth onramp is the same filter time-reversed — run backward from the
# first commits — but steeper, half-life ONRAMP_HALF_LIFE_DAYS (Joseph: the
# forward rate made it too gentle). Work starts before the first commit, in
# proportion to how the project opened.
# History is fetched SMOOTH_WARMUP_DAYS past the oldest shown day so the
# oldest edge isn't cold-started. --strict shows raw counts with no onramp.
SMOOTH_HALF_LIFE_DAYS = 3
SMOOTH_CARRY = 0.5 ** (1.0 / SMOOTH_HALF_LIFE_DAYS)
SMOOTH_FLOOR = 0.5
SMOOTH_WARMUP_DAYS = 8 * SMOOTH_HALF_LIFE_DAYS  # residual carry 1/256
ONRAMP_HALF_LIFE_DAYS = SMOOTH_HALF_LIFE_DAYS / 3
ONRAMP_CARRY = 0.5 ** (1.0 / ONRAMP_HALF_LIFE_DAYS)
ONRAMP_SOURCE_DAYS = math.ceil(8 * ONRAMP_HALF_LIFE_DAYS)  # residual 1/256
